   "created_at": "2012-11-04T19:33:25+00:00",
   "owner_id": "580995252",
   "owner_name": "Dan Frank",
   "platform": "facebook",
   "post_caption": "So much God talk on here today. It's so easy to be swept away from reality with the infinite comfort and myriad luxuries that religion offers. Further, the consolation that we seek from a deity is quite real to many, if not all, of those who are struggling and need to contextualize their existence as something bigger. \n\nBut none of this matters when you consider how the world works from a scientific perspective. To put it simply, we live in a world where everything works exactly as it should...governed by mathematically-sound physical properties, behaving without exception. This concept  directly opposes the notion of a world in which 'miracles' can occur, and as you would expect there has never been a proven miracle, or even an anomaly that would suggest divine intervention. It may seem to be a bleak or boring mindset, but 100% of the evidence corroborates it and every day we become more competent in understanding the minutiae of how it all works. \n\nIf God does exist, his only success has been to completely cover up any evidence that leads to a rational explanation of himself.",
   "post_created_at": {
    "user_local": "2012-11-04T14:33:25.000-05:00",
    "user_timezone": "America/New_York",
    "utc": "2012-11-04T19:33:25.000Z"
   },
